$test['Animals'] = 'A snow leopard moves diagonally down a rocky slope rather than posing for a portrait. Black and Grey Realism resolves the head and shoulders while the spotted body progressively disappears into broken snow and untouched skin'
$cats['Animals']['Animals Wild Animals'] = @('A snow leopard moves diagonally down a rocky slope rather than posing for a portrait. Black and Grey Realism resolves the head and shoulders while the spotted body progressively disappears into broken snow and untouched skin','A massive African elephant walks toward the viewer through airborne dust. The trunk hangs naturally forward while one ear catches strong side light and the distant legs dissolve into atmosphere','A red fox turns away and disappears into winter grass. Burnt orange Colour Realism remains concentrated around the head and shoulders while the tail and environment become loose painterly marks','A silverback gorilla moves forward on all fours with enormous shoulders and hands defining the composition. Deep Black and Grey values emphasize mass skin texture and physical weight without making the animal roar at the viewer','A giraffe uses the entire vertical length of the calf. Its head turns slightly while the long neck descends naturally with selective Colour Realism and loose geometric fragments appearing within the coat pattern','A wild bison moves through blowing snow with most of its body hidden by weather. Dense black around the head and shoulder contrasts against nearly untouched skin surrounding the animal','An orangutan hangs from a branch with one long arm extending far above the head. Rich rust-colored fur is treated through loose Illustrative strokes while the intelligent face remains realistically resolved','A rhinoceros walks through shallow water from a low viewpoint. The enormous head and horn dominate the foreground while reflected ripples distort the lower legs','A zebra turns sharply while running causing the stripe pattern to bend around the body and become increasingly abstract toward the hindquarters','A moose stands waist-deep in dark water at dawn. The antlers become the widest element while the reflection below breaks into Dotwork and negative skin')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Predators'] = @('A lioness stalks low through tall grass rather than presenting a conventional lion portrait. Only the eyes shoulders and parts of the back break through the vegetation','A jaguar moves through dense shadow with most of its black and gold body partially obscured. Selected rosettes remain highly realistic while others dissolve into Dotwork darkness','A great white shark emerges from almost absolute black water. The animal is initially visible only through the pale underside eye and narrow highlights along the nose','A timber wolf runs through deep snow with its head low and ears back. Sketch movement lines preserve earlier leg positions while the final body resolves through Black and Grey Realism','A tiger moves through tall reeds with only sections of orange body visible between them. The natural stripes interact with the vertical plants until animal and environment become one composition','A peregrine falcon drops toward prey in an extreme vertical dive. Wings compress tightly against the body while the background becomes streaked atmospheric movement','A crocodile is viewed directly from above while swimming. Only the armored back tail and eyes break the dark water allowing the animals long anatomy to define the tattoo','A polar bear emerges from blowing white snow using almost no ink for the body itself. Black nose eyes mouth and carefully controlled grey shadow cause natural skin to become the animal','A spotted hyena walks through darkness carrying the intensity of a real predator rather than a caricature. The heavy neck sloping back and scarred muzzle remain anatomically honest','A python constricts around unseen prey creating a powerful series of overlapping muscular coils. Colour Realism preserves the scale pattern while deep shadow between coils creates extraordinary dimensionality')
$cats['Animals']['Animals In Motion'] = @('A cheetah reaches full sprint with the spine dramatically flexed and all four legs moving through different stages of the stride. Sketch studies around the final animal make speed itself visible','A black stallion gallops across the thigh with mane and tail exploding backward into broad Blackwork gestures. The head and muscular chest remain anatomically detailed','A mountain goat leaps between two rock faces with empty skin forming the gap beneath it. The entire tattoo is built around the suspended instant before landing','A kangaroo is captured mid-bound with the long tail balancing the body and powerful hind legs extended. Loose red-earth Watercolour trails behind the movement','A salmon fights upstream through turbulent water. The body bends against the current while Japanese-influenced water movement wraps around the calf without turning the fish into a Japanese tattoo by default','A hare changes direction at full speed. Multiple faint Sketch positions show the turn while one final body resolves sharply with ears thrown backward','A wild boar charges through brush with the head low and shoulders driving forward. Earth and vegetation explode outward rather than framing a static animal portrait','A dolphin breaks the water surface at speed with the body twisting naturally rather than performing a decorative leap. Sunlight beneath the water creates turquoise Colour Realism across the lower body','A leopard jumps downward from a branch toward the viewer. Extreme foreshortening makes the front paws larger while the long body compresses into the background','A herd of wild horses runs through dust but only three animals receive significant detail. The remaining herd becomes atmospheric silhouettes so movement and scale dominate over individual portraits')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Wings and Flight'] = @('A raven lands with both wings braking hard and the tail spread beneath it. Deep Blackwork feathers alternate with untouched skin so the bird feels enormous without becoming a solid black mass','A barn owl strikes downward with talons extended. The pale face remains nearly untouched skin while the wings become layered Dotwork shadow','A great blue heron lifts from shallow water. Its extremely long legs trail behind while wings rise vertically through the composition and small droplets remain suspended below','A bearded vulture flies in profile with enormous wings following the shoulder and upper back. Rust cream and black natural coloration creates a striking Colour Realism palette','A flock of flamingos is seen from directly above over turquoise water. Their pink bodies form an organic moving pattern rather than a row of individual bird portraits','A golden eagle banks sharply through a turn with one wing dramatically foreshortened and the opposite wing extended across the chest','A hummingbird hovers beside a flower but the wings are rendered through several translucent movement positions rather than frozen detail','A pelican dives vertically toward the ocean with its wings folding backward. The long beak and aerodynamic body create a completely different bird composition from the usual wings-spread pose','A bat turns in flight with one wing coming toward the viewer and the opposite wing receding. Deep burgundy and black create a rich nocturnal palette without pushing the design into Horror','A peacock turns away while opening only part of its tail. The eye patterns transition gradually from Colour Realism into abstract jewel-like shapes around the shoulder')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Ocean and Deep Water'] = @('A blue whale descends vertically into increasingly dark water with a tiny diver far above it. Scale becomes the entire idea making the whale feel unimaginably large','An orca turns beneath the surface with the black body becoming a natural Blackwork composition and the white markings created primarily from untouched skin','A giant Pacific octopus wraps across the shoulder and upper arm. The head occupies the shoulder while tentacles independently follow the arm disappearing and reappearing around the anatomy','A translucent jellyfish drifts downward with soft Colour Realism in violet cobalt and pale pink. Tentacles become increasingly Fine Line as they descend toward the wrist','A hammerhead shark is seen from above while turning through deep blue water. The unmistakable head shape creates the composition while sunlight fades rapidly beneath the animal','A manta ray passes overhead from the viewpoint of someone underwater. Its enormous dark silhouette dominates while thin shafts of sunlight break around the wings','A giant squid rises from absolute darkness with only portions of the mantle eye and twisting arms illuminated by cold blue light','A seahorse is enlarged dramatically and rendered as an anatomical Colour Realism study. Tiny plates ridges and translucent fins make the familiar creature appear almost alien','A sea turtle swims downward through sunlit water. The shell receives realistic detail while the surrounding light breaks into geometric caustic patterns across the body','A whale skeleton rests on the abyssal seafloor with tiny deep-sea organisms gathering around it. The bones disappear gradually into black water rather than becoming a conventional skeleton tattoo')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Scales Armor and Strange Creatures'] = @('A chameleon grips a branch while its skin transitions from natural Colour Realism into increasingly abstract color fields. One rotating eye remains sharply realistic','A pangolin curls partially around itself allowing the overlapping armor scales to become the visual focus. Fine Dotwork shadow between plates creates extraordinary depth','A rattlesnake moves across the forearm in a loose S curve rather than a traditional coiled strike. The rattle receives almost scientific detail while the body wraps naturally around the anatomy','A poison dart frog sits half submerged on a wet leaf. Electric natural blue and black patterning contrasts with deep emerald surroundings and reflective droplets','A Komodo dragon walks directly across the calf with heavy legs and low body emphasizing prehistoric anatomy. Dust rises around the feet while the tongue catches a tiny highlight','A praying mantis turns its triangular head toward the viewer while the body remains in profile. Fine Line anatomy combines with emerald Colour Realism concentrated around the forelegs','A rhinoceros beetle is enlarged dramatically with the shell rendered in iridescent emerald and violet. The horn and armored body create an almost mechanical silhouette','A giant centipede travels around the forearm with dozens of legs following the curvature rather than sitting flat. Deep red and black create a controlled unsettling palette','An axolotl floats through dark water with delicate external gills rendered in translucent pink. The animal remains anatomically natural rather than becoming a cute mascot','A Tyrannosaurus is reconstructed as a living animal moving through a humid prehistoric environment. Anatomical credibility and believable mass matter more than creating a movie monster')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Animal and Environment'] = @('A coyote stands on a dry California ridge at dusk with the animal seen mostly in silhouette. A narrow band of warm sky separates its ears and back from the surrounding darkness','A brown bear stands chest-deep in a rushing river as salmon move beneath the surface. Water divides the composition so the viewer simultaneously sees above and below','A snow monkey sits in falling snow beside steaming water. The face and wet fur remain realistic while atmosphere occupies as much visual importance as the animal','An alligator rests almost completely submerged in swamp water. Only eyes nostrils and sections of armored back remain visible while cypress reflections create vertical distortion around it','A mountain lion crosses a rocky desert ledge at night. Moonlight catches only the spine shoulders and tail while most of the animal disappears into the surrounding rock','A crane stands in shallow marsh water with its reflection broken by ripples. Fine Line reeds and soft Watercolour atmosphere create a quiet environment without overwhelming the bird','A herd of elephants crosses a dusty plain in the distance while one enormous foreground elephant occupies the lower composition. Atmospheric scale makes the scene feel expansive rather than photographic','A black bear climbs through a dense pine forest. Portions of the animal disappear behind trunks so the forest and bear visually interlock instead of becoming subject and background','A green sea turtle moves through a coral environment where only selected coral receives saturated color. The turtle remains the visual anchor while the reef creates depth','A red stag stands in morning fog with the antlers disappearing into bare tree branches. At several points it becomes difficult to tell where antler ends and forest begins')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Black Dark and Untamed'] = @('A black panther emerges from a nearly solid Blackwork field. Only the eyes nose teeth and several highlights across the shoulders reveal the animal','A raven stands on the remains of a large animal in a bleak landscape. The scene is treated as stark Black and Grey nature rather than Gothic fantasy with the raven alert and completely alive','A rattlesnake sheds its skin. The living head and body move forward while the translucent abandoned skin retains the ghostlike shape of the former animal behind it','A dead bird lies with one wing open. Individual feathers gradually lift from the body and become a distant flock creating transformation without using supernatural symbols','A wolf moves through a near-white snowstorm. Almost the entire body is lost except for dark eyes nose and intermittent areas of wet fur','A skeletal horse begins as exposed bone at the rear and progressively becomes muscle skin and a fully living horse as it moves forward into a gallop','A vulture opens its wings over a dark landscape with the bald head turned sharply toward the viewer. Heavy black feather masses make the design graphic and unapologetically severe','A shark emerges from black water with another smaller shark barely visible deeper behind it. The design relies on what cannot be seen as much as what can','A stag skull remains tangled in roots and forest growth. Moss fungi and small new plants emerge through the bone so death appears as part of the natural environment rather than Horror decoration','A moth spreads its wings in deep Blackwork but subtle skeletal structures appear inside the wing pattern as though bone and insect anatomy have merged')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Animal Transformed Into Art'] = @('A leopard begins in Colour Realism at the face. Moving backward the rosettes detach from the fur and progressively become Dotwork abstract circles and finally empty skin','A raven begins as anatomically realistic at the head and chest while one enormous wing transforms into a sweeping black brushstroke that follows the shoulder blade','A stags head remains realistic while the antlers progressively reorganize into precise Geometric structures that spread naturally across the upper back','A humpback whale appears to contain a storm within its body. The outer anatomy remains unmistakably whale while clouds lightning and turbulent ocean exist inside the silhouette','A zebras stripes detach from the body as it moves becoming flowing black ribbons that wrap around the arm. The animal remains recognizable even as its pattern escapes it','A cobra is rendered realistically at the head while the scales gradually transform into ornamental geometry down the body. The transition follows the natural scale grid rather than being divided into two halves','A jellyfish becomes a living Watercolour painting. The bell remains translucent and believable while tentacles dissolve into pigment blooms drips and soft color diffusion','A rhinoceros appears cracked like an ancient landscape. Instead of exposing machinery or fantasy material the fissures contain tiny cliffs dry riverbeds and geological layers','A peacocks feather eyes progressively become celestial bodies as the tail expands. The bird remains biologically recognizable while the pattern creates the surreal transformation','A black stallion is built from aggressive Sketch lines charcoal darkness and abandoned anatomical studies. The final horse appears to emerge from the visible process of drawing it')
$cats['Animals']['Animals Push Animals'] = @('A giant octopus takes ownership of the entire shoulder and arm. The head occupies the shoulder while each tentacle has a distinct anatomical route some wrapping the bicep some disappearing behind the arm and others reappearing toward the forearm. The suckers change dramatically in scale through perspective. Deep crimson violet and black make the animal feel intelligent and physically present rather than decorative','A snow leopard moves across the womans back in near silence. The head and shoulders are resolved in Black and Grey Realism while the body disappears into a blizzard of Dotwork and untouched skin. The tail crosses the spine and reappears faintly on the opposite side making the body part of the disappearance','A massive crocodile is seen from directly above traveling down the mans leg. The head begins high on the thigh armored back follows the knee and the tail bends naturally around the calf. Sections disappear beneath black water so the anatomy of the leg becomes the river','A blue whale and calf descend through deep ocean across the womans back. The calf remains near the mothers body while their scale is established by a tiny distant diver and shafts of surface light far above. Color transitions from luminous blue near the shoulders to nearly absolute black lower in the composition','A lioness launches through tall grass toward unseen prey. Her nearest paw projects dramatically toward the viewer while the body compresses into the grass behind it. Instead of a regal portrait the tattoo captures the animal in the violent precision of the hunt','A giant raven occupies the mans chest and shoulder with one wing sweeping across the chest and the other wrapping around the shoulder. The head remains realistic but feathers progressively become Blackwork Sketch Dotwork and raw brush gestures as they travel outward. The transitions happen organically through feather structure rather than in separate style sections','A hammerhead shark passes above the viewer while an enormous school of smaller fish parts around its silhouette. The shark itself remains calm and anatomically realistic. Deep turquoise light above fades into navy and black below while the fish create movement and scale around the predator','A stag stands in a dark forest while its enormous antlers gradually become the forest canopy itself. Branches antlers and roots repeat the same structural language until the animal appears inseparable from the environment. Small areas of amber dawn light break through the black composition','A living Tyrannosaurus moves through a prehistoric forest during heavy rain. The animal is treated as an enormous biological creature rather than a movie monster. Mud muscle wet skin atmospheric distance and vegetation establish scale while the head turns slightly toward the viewer. A smaller feathered dinosaur moves through vegetation below making the ecosystem feel alive rather than turning the piece into a single dinosaur portrait','Create an extraordinary animal composition in which a massive manta ray passes above a tiny submerged city. The ray remains anatomically believable but its enormous wings extend across the upper back as though the human body is the ocean surface seen from below. Rays of turquoise light break around the animal. Schools of fish move between distant buildings. One wing progressively dissolves into abstract oceanic geometry while the opposite wing remains realistic. The contrast in scale should make the animal feel almost impossible without turning it into a fantasy creature. The manta ray remains the unquestioned hero')
$b['A snow leopard moves diagonally down a rocky slope rather than posing for a portrait. Black and Grey Realism resolves the head and shoulders while the spotted body progressively disappears into broken snow and untouched skin'] = 'The tattoo: A snow leopard moves diagonally down a rocky slope rather than posing for a portrait. Black and Grey Realism resolves the head and shoulders while the spotted body progressively disappears into broken snow and untouched skin. Silent, elusive, powerful. Create exceptional contemporary tattoo inspiration centered on animals. ANIMALS = WHAT I LOVE. This category is about fascination with animals themselves. Their movement. Anatomy. Behavior. Texture. Environment. Power. Beauty. Strangeness. Violence. Scale. Survival. DO NOT GENERATE AN ANIMAL PORTRAIT WHEN AN ANIMAL EXPERIENCE WOULD BE MORE INTERESTING. Do not default to a centered animal head looking directly at the viewer. Show animals behaving like animals. Running. Hunting. Swimming. Diving. Flying. Landing. Climbing. Stalking. Feeding. Fighting. Resting. Migrating. Shedding. Emerging. Disappearing. Turning. Striking. Escaping. Moving through environments. DO NOT MAKE THE ANIMAL BEAUTIFUL BY DEFAULT. MAKE IT ALIVE. Beauty is welcome. But beauty is not the requirement. Animals can be: Elegant. Violent. Quiet. Predatory. Ugly. Strange. Ancient. Fragile. Massive. Graceful. Armored. Wet. Dirty. Wounded. Hidden. Colorful. Dark. Terrifying. Peaceful. Do not romanticize every animal. Do not turn every predator into a noble portrait. Do not turn every bird into wings spread symmetrically. Do not turn every snake into a decorative coil. Do not turn every ocean animal into a peaceful blue scene. Do not turn every wildlife tattoo into flowers surrounding an animal head. ROTATE SPECIES AGGRESSIVELY. Include familiar animals. Lion. Lioness. Tiger. Leopard. Jaguar. Panther. Wolf. Fox. Coyote. Bear. Polar bear. Elephant. Gorilla. Orangutan. Rhinoceros. Giraffe. Zebra. Stag. Moose. Bison. Ram. Mountain goat. Wild horse. Wild boar. But do not allow familiar animals to consume the category. Explore birds. Raven. Crow. Eagle. Falcon. Owl. Heron. Crane. Pelican. Flamingo. Hummingbird. Vulture. Peacock. Bat. Explore ocean life. Great white shark. Hammerhead shark. Whale. Orca. Dolphin. Manta ray. Octopus. Squid. Jellyfish. Sea turtle. Seahorse. Deep-sea animals. Explore reptiles and amphibians. Crocodile. Alligator. Cobra. Python. Rattlesnake. Chameleon. Iguana. Komodo dragon. Tortoise. Frog. Salamander. Explore strange and overlooked animals. Pangolin. Axolotl. Praying mantis. Beetles. Cicadas. Spiders. Scorpions. Centipedes. Rare regional wildlife. Explore prehistoric animals when appropriate. Treat them as animals rather than fantasy monsters. Use current scientific understanding when anatomical credibility matters. THE STYLE IS NOT FIXED. Use the full world of tattooing. Realism. Black and Grey Realism. Colour Realism. Fine Line. Sketch. Dotwork. Blackwork. Watercolour. Illustrative. Geometric. Japanese. American Traditional. Neo-Traditional. New School. Negative Space. Surrealism. And intelligent hybrids. Do not rotate styles mechanically. Ask what the animal gives the artist. Fur can become brushwork. Feathers can become Blackwork. Scales can become geometry. Spots can become Dotwork. Stripes can become abstraction. Tentacles can become body flow. Wings can become large negative-space compositions. Shells and armor can become texture studies. Translucent animals can become Colour Realism and Watercolour. White animals can be created through untouched skin. Black animals can emerge from darkness. THE ANIMALS ANATOMY SHOULD HELP DESIGN THE TATTOO. A snake can wrap. An octopus can travel around anatomy. A manta ray can own a back. A bird can use the shoulder blades. A giraffe can use vertical anatomy. A crocodile can travel down a leg. A whale can establish enormous scale. A stag can expand through antlers. A jellyfish can descend through long placements. A big cat can move across the thigh. A raven can use shoulder and chest. Do not put every animal inside a rectangular scene. Allow environment and animal to interlock. Use: Snow. Water. Fog. Dust. Rain. Grass. Forest. Rock. Desert. Ocean. Swamp. Night. Fire. Wind. Light. Shadow. Environment should reveal something about the animal. It should not simply become decorative background. REGIONAL WILDLIFE MATTERS. People may love animals because those animals belong to where they are from. Do not assume every animal requires universal symbolism. A coyote can matter because someone grew up hearing coyotes. A pelican can matter because someone lives on the coast. An alligator can matter because it belongs to someones landscape. A whale can matter because someone sees them migrate. The animal does not need a dictionary meaning to deserve a tattoo. DO NOT AUTOMATICALLY ASSIGN CANNED SYMBOLISM. Lion does not automatically mean courage. Wolf does not automatically mean loyalty. Owl does not automatically mean wisdom. Snake does not automatically mean rebirth. If symbolism is important, let the customer define it or explain genuine cultural associations accurately. Nature can become dark without becoming Horror. Explore: Predation. Death. Decay. Shedding. Skeletons. Migration. Survival. Carcasses. Scavengers. Deep water. Darkness. Injury. Transformation. Weather. Extinction. Life cycles. Keep the animal world central. Do not add skulls and demons simply to make an animal tattoo darker. NATURE ALREADY CONTAINS DARKNESS. Surrealism is welcome when the animal remains the hero. A whale can contain a storm. A stags antlers can become forest. A leopards spots can become stars. A zebras stripes can leave its body. A birds wings can contain night. A rhinoceros can become landscape. A manta ray can pass over an impossible city. A snake can become smoke. But do not bury the animal beneath an unrelated concept. The viewer should still think: WHAT AN INCREDIBLE ANIMAL TATTOO. Design for actual human anatomy. Use the body. Wrap when the animal gives you wrapping anatomy. Stretch when the animal gives you length. Expand when the animal gives you wings. Use joints when movement benefits from them. Use broad surfaces for scale. Use small placements for delicate animals. Use large placements only when the concept earns them. Do not make everything enormous. Do not make everything tiny. Do not make everything realistic. Do not make everything Blackwork. Do not make everything colorful. Do not make everything dark. Do not make everything pretty. Do not make everything safe. THE CATEGORY TELLS US THE DOORWAY. IT DOES NOT TELL US HOW FAR WE ARE ALLOWED TO GO ONCE WE ARE INSIDE. THE ANIMAL IS THE HERO. THE ART CAN GO ANYWHERE. In the right panel it is on a woman, outer thigh'
